# This file is a reference only. Real secrets are never stored in a committed file —
# set them with `wrangler secret put <NAME>` (see DEPLOY.md).
#
# Secrets required:
#   KORA_SECRET_KEY   - Korapay secret key (server-side only, never exposed to the browser)
#   JWT_SECRET         - random 32+ byte string used to sign session/PIN tokens
#   RESEND_API_KEY     - Resend API key for sending OTP verification emails
#   ADMIN_API_KEY       - a long random string; required as X-Admin-Key header to view webhook logs
#
# Plain vars (in wrangler.jsonc, not secret):
#   KORA_PUBLIC_KEY    - Korapay public key, safe to expose client-side
#   ALLOWED_ORIGIN      - https://mikpal.com (locks down CSRF checks)
#   COOKIE_DOMAIN        - mikpal.com
#   FROM_EMAIL            - "MIKPAL <no-reply@mikpal.com>" (must be a Resend-verified domain)
